# Files excluded from a Vercel deployment.
#
# The GitHub integration only ever sees committed files, and .gitignore already
# keeps the large data directories out of the repository. This matters most for
# `vercel --prod` from a terminal, which deploys the working directory instead:
# without this file every CLI deploy would upload ~450 MB of Input/, history/
# and updating_files/.
#
# IMPORTANT: this only decides what gets *uploaded*. Vercel's Python builder
# then globs the entire uploaded tree into the function (it does not tree-shake
# and it ignores `includeFiles` completely), so do not rely on this to keep a
# file out of the function bundle - only out of the upload.

# --- secrets ---
# Patterns without a slash match at any depth, so `.env.*` also covers
# liveapp/.env. The negation keeps the committed template.
.env
.env.*
liveapp/.env
liveapp/seed_users.json
!liveapp/.env.example

# --- source data and ETL outputs: build machine only (~450 MB) ---
Input/
updating_files/
output/
history/
liveapp/storage/
*.xlsx
*.xls
*.csv
*.parquet
*.zip

# --- local Python artefacts ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# --- VCS and deployment internals ---
.git/
.gitignore
.vercel/

# --- docs: useful on GitHub, dead weight in the bundle ---
DEPLOYMENT.md
LIVE_DATABASE_DASHBOARD.md
PROCESS_SUMMARY.md
liveapp/README.md

# KEEP (required at runtime):
#   api/**                     the function entrypoint
#   liveapp/app/**             the FastAPI application
#   liveapp/frontend/**        login shell + admin panel
#   liveapp/main.py            local dev launcher
#   liveapp/run_process.py     local ETL launcher
#   liveapp/requirements.txt   local dependency set
#   _dashboard_template.html   the dashboard UI, served at /_dashboard_template.html
#   build_dashboard.py         imported by liveapp/app/services/builder.py
#   requirements.txt           the dependency set Vercel installs